kind: fix

When GJK stops sure the shapes overlap (status Collision: its simplex came
within tolerance of the origin) and no depth was asked for, coal skipped EPA
but returned GJK's last distance, a sliver up to its tolerance (1e-6) above
0. ShapeShapeCollide and the mesh/shape collision leaves then subtract the
margin from that and compare it to collision_distance_threshold (1e-12 by
default), so an overlap, however deep, could be reported as no contact.
It happens mostly between like or symmetric solids whose GJK starts near
the line between their centers: trimkit's collides missed 2 of 2222
touching pairs over 300 talos configurations and 2 of 1452 over 200 g1
ones at the request defaults, overlapping by up to 2.5 mm, and once GJK
started between box centers, 11 pairs 0.06 to 1.7 deep among 40 placements
of 60 copies of one sphere. The distance is 0, as overlapping shapes are.
Covered by check/tests/test_collision.py::test_overlapping_convex_solids_collide.
Not reported upstream yet; the same lines are in coal devel as pinned.

--- a/include/coal/narrowphase/narrowphase.h
+++ b/include/coal/narrowphase/narrowphase.h
@@ -756,7 +756,12 @@
     // this->cached_guess = this->gjk.ray;
     this->support_func_cached_guess = this->gjk.support_hint;
 
-    distance = Scalar(this->gjk.distance);
+    //// TRIMKIT PATCH: fix.gjk-collision-distance
+    // GJK said the shapes overlap: they are 0 apart, not the sliver its
+    // simplex stopped short of the origin by, which collision then compared
+    // to its threshold as a gap and reported no contact
+    distance = Scalar(0);
+    //// TRIMKIT END PATCH
     p1 = p2 = normal = Vec3s::Constant(std::numeric_limits<Scalar>::max());
   }
 
